{"name":"Radome Tan","hex":"#f1c7a1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"radome","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of radar dome."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radome"},{"term":"tan","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["The trigonometric function tangent."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Tangale."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tan"}],"entries":[{"title":"Radome","blocks":[{"text":"A radome is a structural, weatherproof enclosure that protects a radar antenna. The radome is constructed of material transparent to radio waves. Radomes protect the antenna from weather and conceal antenna electronic equipment from view. They also protect nearby personnel from being accidentally struck by quickly rotating antennas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Navy-Radome.jpg/330px-Navy-Radome.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radome","wikidata":"Q659994"},{"title":"Tan (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Tan is a pale tone of brown. The name is derived from tannum used in the tanning of leather."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Chestnut_Oak_Bark.jpg/330px-Chestnut_Oak_Bark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tan_(color)","wikidata":"Q1670336"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/HMS_Daring_SAMPSON_is_a_multi-function_AESA_radar.jpg/500px-HMS_Daring_SAMPSON_is_a_multi-function_AESA_radar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/HMS_Daring_SAMPSON_is_a_multi-function_AESA_radar.jpg/1280px-HMS_Daring_SAMPSON_is_a_multi-function_AESA_radar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src"